course: dictionary
lesson: 8084
title: Remarkable: amazing and worth noticing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Remarkable is a word for things that stand out. Something remarkable is unusual or special, so people notice it and talk about it. «Three royal marriages are still remarkable.» Even if a claim is too much, three royal marriages are still unusual enough to stand out.
explain: Look at the words around remarkable to check its meaning. In stories, a remarkable person or event is one that stands out. In science and history, a remarkable discovery is surprising and important. In school reports, remarkable progress is great praise.
explain: Remarkable is often used in phrases such as a remarkable achievement and remarkably good. Try swapping in amazing or impressive. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found a good match.
fact: Remarkable means unusual or special, in a way that people notice.
fact: Remarkable is an adjective. Its forms are remarkable, more remarkable and most remarkable.
fact: «Remarkable» can mean amazing or impressive, as in «a remarkable achievement».
fact: In «His son Yaroslav the Wise built Saint Sophia, gathered books, began the law code Ruska Pravda and married his daughters to kings», the author shows why his life was remarkable.
fact: Remarkably is the adverb form, as in «remarkably good».
exercise: «Three royal marriages are still remarkable.» What does remarkable mean in this sentence? | Forgotten by most people | *Unusual and worth noticing | Boring and ordinary | Quiet and sad
exercise: A teacher writes, «Your progress this term has been remarkable.» What does the teacher mean? | You must do it again | Your progress is slow | *Your progress is impressive and great | You have stopped trying
exercise: Danylo says «father-in-law of all Europe» is too much. What does this tell you about his view? | He thinks Yaroslav was ordinary | He thinks it is completely true | *He thinks the claim goes too far | He thinks the marriages were boring
test: Which phrase best matches a remarkable achievement? | a late bus | an ordinary day at school | *an amazing feat that people talk about | a small tidy desk
test: Which word means the same as remarkable? | tiny | *impressive | dull | ordinary
exam: Mia says a remarkable discovery is a boring one. Is she right? | *No, remarkable means surprising and important | Only if the discovery is tiny | It depends on the weather | Yes, remarkable means dull and ordinary
